格式示例（仅结构，不是来源事实）：evidence:[{"paragraph_id":"p3s1","fact":"该片段支持的中文转述"}]。请从本次真实输入挑选编号。","role":"system"},{"content":"{"metadata":{"description":"Multi-agent DeepSeek Harness workbench with switchable Pi, OpenAI Codex, Claude Code, and native DeepSeek Agent Loops.","id":"gh:1332196118","install_available":false,"language":"TypeScript","name":"LoopWithAI","slug":"loopwithai/LoopWithAI","topics":["agent-loop","ai-agent","ai-coding","claude-code","codex","coding-agent","cordis","deepseek","deepseek-harness","developer-tools","dsh-plugin","llm","local-first","multi-agent","openai-codex","pi-coding-agent","typescript"]},"paragraphs":[{"id":"p1s1","text":"Multi-agent DeepSeek Harness workbench with switchable Pi, OpenAI Codex, Claude Code, and native Dee"},{"id":"p1s2","text":"ek Harness workbench with switchable Pi, OpenAI Codex, Claude Code, and native DeepSeek Agent Loops."},{"id":"p2s1","text":"LoopWithAI\nA multi-agent workbench for DeepSeek Harness.\nRun Pi, OpenAI Codex, Claude Code, or the n"},{"id":"p2s2","text":"ative DeepSeek Agent Loop in one local Web UI."},{"id":"p3s1","text":"简体中文"},{"id":"p4s1","text":"DeepSeek Harness"},{"id":"p5s1","text":"Quick start"},{"id":"p6s1","text":"LoopWithAI turns DeepSeek Harness into a local multi-agent coding workbench. It keeps Harness's nati"},{"id":"p6s2","text":"ve Cordis plugin architecture and makes its Agent Loop replaceable, so you can switch between **Pi C"},{"id":"p6s3","text":"oding Agent**, **OpenAI Codex**, **Claude Code**, and the original **DeepSeek Agent Loop** without a"},{"id":"p6s4","text":"dding an ACP gateway or a separate driver layer."},{"id":"p7s1","text":"Pi is the default Agent. Every runtime keeps its native model access, tools, approvals, MCP configur"},{"id":"p7s2","text":"ation, skills/extensions, and local authentication."},{"id":"p8s1","text":"> DeepSeek Harness is currently a developer preview. LoopWithAI follows its plugin APIs closely, so "},{"id":"p8s2","text":"breaking upstream changes may require an update."},{"id":"p9s1","text":"## Why LoopWithAI"},{"id":"p10s1","text":"- **One DeepSeek Harness, multiple Agents** — change the active Agent Loop from the composer instead"},{"id":"p10s2","text":" of moving between separate terminal apps.\n- **Native integrations** — Pi uses its TypeScript SDK, C"},{"id":"p10s3","text":"odex uses `codex app-server`, Claude Code uses the Agent SDK, and DeepSeek uses Harness's original A"},{"id":"p10s4","text":"gent Loop.\n- **Models and Thinking controls** — choose the provider/model and supported reasoning le"},{"id":"p10s5","text":"vel directly beside the prompt.\n- **Full coding tools** — read, bash, edit, write, project instructi"},{"id":"p10s6","text":"ons, skills, extensions, MCP servers, and approval flows remain available where the selected Agent s"},{"id":"p10s7","text":"upports them.\n- **Local-first credentials and sessions** — tokens remain in the native Pi, Codex, Cl"},{"id":"p10s8","text":"aude Code, or environment stores. LoopWithAI does not run a hosted credential gateway.\n- **Workspace"},{"id":"p10s9","text":" continuity** — reopen the last Workspace automatically; a fresh install starts at `~/.lwa/workspace"},{"id":"p10s10","text":"`.\n- **Proxy support** — use terminal environment variables, the macOS system proxy/Clash, a manual "},{"id":"p10s11","text":"HTTP proxy, or force direct connections.\n- **Vite development workflow** — client-side workbench con"},{"id":"p10s12","text":"trols update with HMR while Harness remains running."},{"id":"p11s1","text":"## Supported Agents"},{"id":"p12s1","text":"| Agent | Integration | Authentication | Native capabilities retained |"},{"id":"p13s1","text":"| **Pi** (default) | `@earendil-works/pi-coding-agent` SDK | Accounts panel, `pi /login`, or `~/.pi/"},{"id":"p13s2","text":"agent` | models/providers, tools, skills, extensions, sessions, Thinking levels |\n| **DeepSeek** | o"},{"id":"p13s3","text":"riginal `@deepseek-ai/dsh-agent-loop` | `DEEPSEEK_API_KEY` and normal Harness settings | original Ha"},{"id":"p13s4","text":"rness Agent Loop and DeepSeek models |\n| **OpenAI Codex** | `codex app-server --stdio` | existing `c"},{"id":"p13s5","text":"odex login` session | tools, MCP, sandbox, approvals, threads, models, reasoning effort |\n| **Claude"},{"id":"p13s6","text":" Code** | `@anthropic-ai/claude-agent-sdk` | existing Claude Code login or Anthropic environment | C"},{"id":"p13s7","text":"laude Code tool preset, settings, skills, plugins, MCP, permissions |"},{"id":"p14s1","text":"LoopWithAI replaces the single process-wide Agent Loop transactionally through Cordis Loader. A blan"},{"id":"p14s2","text":"k conversation switches immediately. If the current conversation already has history, the UI asks fo"},{"id":"p14s3","text":"r confirmation and opens a new conversation in the same Workspace, preventing a silent mid-session r"},{"id":"p14s4","text":" and opens a new conversation in the same Workspace, preventing a silent mid-session runtime change."},{"id":"p15s1","text":"## Quick start"},{"id":"p16s1","text":"Requirements:"},{"id":"p17s1","text":"- Node.js 24 or newer\n- npm and Git\n- credentials for whichever Agent you want to use"},{"id":"p18s1","text":"Clone, install, and start:"},{"id":"p19s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p20s1","text":"Or use one shell command:"},{"id":"p21s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p22s1","text":"Open http://127.0.0.1:3210. `npm run dev` also starts the Vite HMR server on port `5174`."},{"id":"p23s1","text":"For a production-style local start without the Vite development server:"},{"id":"p24s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p25s1","text":"## Sign in to an Agent"},{"id":"p26s1","text":"### Pi"},{"id":"p27s1","text":"Select **Pi**, then open **Accounts** beside the composer. The Web flow supports the OAuth providers"},{"id":"p27s2","text":" exposed by Pi, including ChatGPT/OpenAI Codex and Anthropic. You can also authenticate in the termi"},{"id":"p27s3","text":"osed by Pi, including ChatGPT/OpenAI Codex and Anthropic. You can also authenticate in the terminal:"},{"id":"p28s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p29s1","text":"Pi continues to own its configuration and credentials under `~/.pi/agent`. LoopWithAI never returns "},{"id":"p29s2","text":"raw tokens to the browser."},{"id":"p30s1","text":"### OpenAI Codex"},{"id":"p31s1","text":"Install and sign in with the official OpenAI Codex CLI, then select **Codex** in LoopWithAI:"},{"id":"p32s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p33s1","text":"LoopWithAI starts `codex app-server --stdio` when needed and reuses the CLI's existing local login. "},{"id":"p33s2","text":"Set `CODEX_BINARY` only if your `codex` executable is not on `PATH`."},{"id":"p34s1","text":"### Claude Code"},{"id":"p35s1","text":"Authenticate with Claude Code normally, then select **Claude Code**:"},{"id":"p36s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p37s1","text":"The runtime uses the Claude Agent SDK and your normal Claude Code settings. Standard Anthropic envir"},{"id":"p37s2","text":"onment credentials also continue to work."},{"id":"p38s1","text":"### Native DeepSeek Agent Loop"},{"id":"p39s1","text":"Export your DeepSeek key before starting LoopWithAI:"},{"id":"p40s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p41s1","text":"Harness also supports its normal credential/settings layers. `DEEPSEEK_BASE_URL` can override the pu"},{"id":"p41s2","text":"blic DeepSeek endpoint when required."},{"id":"p42s1","text":"## Using the workbench"},{"id":"p43s1","text":"1. Choose or add a Workspace. On startup, LoopWithAI restores the last valid Workspace; otherwise it"},{"id":"p43s2","text":" creates `~/.lwa/workspace` using the operating system's home directory.\n2. Select **Pi**, **DeepSee"},{"id":"p43s3","text":"k**, **Codex**, or **Claude Code** in the composer.\n3. Select an available model and provider.\n[该节后续"},{"id":"p43s4","text":", **Codex**, or **Claude Code** in the composer.\n3. Select an available model and provider.\n[该节后续省略]"},{"id":"p44s1","text":"## Architecture"},{"id":"p45s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p46s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p47s1","text":"The older event-sourced Loop prototype remains parked under `apps/web` and `packages/core`; it is no"},{"id":"p47s2","text":"t the default product surface and is not part of the current development focus."},{"id":"p48s1","text":"## Security and privacy"},{"id":"p49s1","text":"- The workbench runs locally and does not proxy Agent traffic through a LoopWithAI cloud service.\n- "},{"id":"p49s2","text":"Runtime credentials remain in their native local stores or environment variables.\n- Credential APIs "},{"id":"p49s3","text":"expose status and safe model metadata, never raw secret values.\n- Tool execution and network access "},{"id":"p49s4","text":"still depend on the selected Agent and the approval mode you choose."}],"truncated":true}","role":"user"}],"model":"MiniMax-M3.1-Flash","reasoning_effort":"low","stream":false}
